WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.216
Hi, I'm Gunwale!

00:00:02.216 --> 00:00:05.918
Intel's AI Playground lets you message your own PC from your phone.

00:00:05.918 --> 00:00:07.153
Here is the path.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:10.635
The trick is direction.

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:13.371
Your PC asks the chat service for messages.

00:00:13.371 --> 00:00:14.397
Nothing connects in.

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:19.709
You type on your phone.

00:00:19.709 --> 00:00:22.096
The message waits on Telegram's or Slack's servers.

00:00:22.516 --> 00:00:26.301
A Python service on your PC holds a request open and collects it.

00:00:26.721 --> 00:00:30.365
The desktop app checks that service every two seconds, over loopback,

00:00:30.365 --> 00:00:31.690
with a secret token.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.332
It runs the turn on local models.

00:00:34.332 --> 00:00:38.140
A small Qwen model plans, and ComfyUI draws on the Arc card.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.363
Replies return the same way.

00:00:40.363 --> 00:00:43.969
Compute stays home; prompts and pictures cross the chat service.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:49.001
Reaching a home PC usually means a forwarded port, a tunnel,

00:00:49.001 --> 00:00:50.250
or a vendor relay.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.749
Home Agent only connects outward, and no Intel server sits in the path.

00:00:56.192 --> 00:00:57.783
Who may talk to it is one number.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:01.437
In setup, you message your bot and press Detect.

00:01:01.437 --> 00:01:03.023
The app reads your chat id.

00:01:03.443 --> 00:01:05.964
Every handler compares each sender against it.

00:01:05.964 --> 00:01:07.764
Slack uses one user id.

00:01:08.185 --> 00:01:10.752
Anyone else is dropped before the model sees a word.

00:01:11.172 --> 00:01:11.752
One catch.

00:01:11.752 --> 00:01:15.523
Detect can pick up a stranger, so check the test message reached you.

00:01:16.967 --> 00:01:21.446
Past the gate, a message drives an agent with tools, like Python inside Blender.

00:01:21.866 --> 00:01:23.475
Tools are on by default.

00:01:23.475 --> 00:01:27.014
Only settings changes and downloads ask first, in the same chat.

00:01:28.592 --> 00:01:31.706
The project's tests pass offline, twenty eight of twenty eight.

00:01:35.517 --> 00:01:36.711
The model stays home.

00:01:36.711 --> 00:01:39.695
The chat, and its tools, belong to whoever holds it.

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:46.436
Outward polling, one id as the key, and a transcript that lives

00:01:46.436 --> 00:01:47.559
with the chat service.

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:50.012
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:50.012 --> 00:01:50.593
I'm Gunwale.

00:01:50.593 --> 00:01:50.883
Bye!
